PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L06U2.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":6,"cefr":"B1b","unit":2,"theme":"The World of Tomorrow","essential_question":"How will technology change the way we live?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS1","title":"Driverless Taxis Will Probably Be Common: will, may, might and the Future Continuous","objectives":["Students will be able to make predictions with different levels of certainty using will, may and might.","Students will be able to use the future continuous for actions in progress at a time in the future.","I can say \"Robots will probably help in hospitals, and they might cook our dinners.\"","I can say \"This time next year, I'll be using new apps.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من التنبؤ بدرجات مختلفة من اليقين باستخدام will وmay وmight.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام المستقبل المستمر لأحداث تكون جارية في وقت محدد في المستقبل.","أستطيع أن أقول Robots will probably help in hospitals, and they might cook our dinners.","أستطيع أن أقول This time next year, I'll be using new apps."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"predict","pos":"verb","ipa":"/prɪˈdɪkt/","definition":"to say what you think will happen in the future","arabic":"يتنبّأ","example":"Scientists predict hotter summers.","image_id":"GV-L06-U2-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS1-W01"},{"word":"invention","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈvɛnʃən/","definition":"a new thing that someone has made or designed","arabic":"اختراع","example":"The phone was an amazing invention.","image_id":"GV-L06-U2-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS1-W02"},{"word":"device","pos":"noun","ipa":"/dɪˈvaɪs/","definition":"a machine or tool made for a special job","arabic":"جهاز","example":"A smartwatch is a small device.","image_id":"GV-L06-U2-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS1-W03"},{"word":"artificial","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˌɑrtəˈfɪʃəl/","definition":"made by people, not natural","arabic":"اصطناعي","example":"Artificial intelligence can recognize faces.","image_id":"GV-L06-U2-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Use will / won't + base verb for predictions you feel sure about. Add definitely (very sure) or probably (quite sure) after will and before won't: Robots will definitely help in hospitals. People probably won't need keys.\nUse may or might + base verb when something is possible but not sure: Robots might cook our dinners. People may not need licenses. (may not / might not – no contraction mayn't.)\nThe future continuous – will be + verb-ing – describes an action that will be in progress at a specific time in the future: This time next year, you'll be using new apps. At 8 p.m. tomorrow, I'll be studying.\nwill definitely > will probably > may / might > probably won't > definitely won't\nwill / may / might + base verb (no \"to\")\nfuture continuous: will be + -ing (in progress at a future time)\nNot: will can / might to / mayn't","examples":["In twenty years, most homes will have solar panels.","Doctors will probably use robots in operations.","We might live in smart houses that talk to us.","People may not go to the office every day.","Cash definitely won't disappear next year.","This time tomorrow, I'll be flying to Riyadh.","At 10 a.m. on Thursday, we'll be taking our science test.","In 2040, my brother will be working as an engineer."],"common_errors":["✗ Robots will to cook our food. → ✓ Robots will cook our food. (will + base verb.)","✗ It might rains tomorrow. → ✓ It might rain tomorrow. (might + base verb.)","✗ I will probably not go. → ✓ I probably won't go. (probably comes before won't.)","✗ This time tomorrow, I will fly to Jeddah. → ✓ This time tomorrow, I'll be flying to Jeddah. (In progress at that time → future continuous.)"],"arabic":"نستخدم will وwon't للتنبؤ الذي نحن متأكدون منه، ونضيف definitely (متأكد جدًّا) أو probably (متأكد إلى حد ما).\nنستخدم may وmight للاحتمال غير المؤكد: Robots might cook our dinners.\nالمستقبل المستمر will be + ing لحدث يكون جاريًا في وقت محدد في المستقبل: This time next year, you'll be using new apps.\nلاحظ مكان probably: will probably، لكن probably won't."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Driverless Taxis Will Probably Be Common: will, may, might and the Future Continuous”. Let’s learn predictions with will / won't (+ definitely, probably), may / might (not); the future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time together.","on_screen":"GV-L06-U2-LS1 | Driverless Taxis Will Probably Be Common: will, may, might and the Future Continuous","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Life in 2050”: What will life be like in 2050? Our class asked a scientist, Dr. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"What will life be like in 2050? Our class asked a scientist, Dr.","visual":"Image GV-L06-U2-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Use will / won't + base verb for predictions you feel sure about. Add definitely (very sure) or probably (quite sure) after will and before won't: Robots will definitely help in hospitals. People probably won't need keys. Use may or might + base verb when something is possible but not sure: Robots might cook our dinners. People may not need licenses. (may not / might not – no contraction mayn't.)","on_screen":"will definitely > will probably > may / might > probably won't > definitely won't • will / may / might + base verb (no \"to\") • future continuous: will be + -ing (in progress at a future time)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. In twenty years, most homes will have solar panels. Doctors will probably use robots in operations. We might live in smart houses that talk to us.","on_screen":"In twenty years, most homes will have solar panels. / Doctors will probably use robots in operations. / We might live in smart houses that talk to us.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Robots will to cook our food.” That’s not right. We say: “Robots will cook our food.” will + base verb.","on_screen":"✗ Robots will to cook our food.   ✓ Robots will cook our food.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"Robots might cook our dinners.\" Is the scientist sure? … Think! … No – it's only possible. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"Robots will probably help in hospitals, and they might cook our dinners.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"Robots will probably help in hospitals, and they might cook our dinners.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: predictions with will / won't (+ definitely, probably), may / might (not); the future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نستخدم will وwon't للتنبؤ الذي نحن متأكدون منه، ونضيف definitely (متأكد جدًّا) أو probably (متأكد إلى حد ما).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Robots will to cook our food. — الصحيح: Robots will cook our food.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول Robots will probably help in hospitals, and they might cook our dinners."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Life in 2050","body":"What will life be like in 2050? Our class asked a scientist, Dr. Huda, to share her predictions.\n\"In 2050, most cars will be electric, and many of them will drive themselves. Driverless taxis will probably be common in our cities. People may not need driving licenses at all!\" she says.\n\"Robots will definitely help in hospitals, and they might even cook our dinners. Artificial intelligence will be in almost every device we use.\"\nWhat about school? \"Students may study with virtual-reality headsets. In fact, this time next year, you'll be using apps that don't exist yet!\"\nDr. Huda believes energy will be cleaner. \"By then, our country will be producing much of its electricity from the sun and the wind.\"\nWill people live on Mars? \"Possibly. A small colony might be living there, but most of us definitely won't move to space!\"\nFinally, she gave us some advice: \"The future isn't only something that happens to you. You'll be building it. So keep learning!\"","word_count":165,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"In the future, most cars ___ electric.","options":["are being will","will being","will be","will to be"],"answer":"will be","explanation":"Sure prediction → will / won't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"تنبؤ مؤكد ← will."},{"q":"It's cloudy. It ___ rain later, but I'm not sure.","options":["will definitely","might","might to","is"],"answer":"might","explanation":"Possible, not sure → may / might (not) + base verb.","explanation_ar":"الاحتمال ← may/might."},{"q":"People ___ need passports for some trips in the future.","options":["probably won't","will probably not to","probably will not to","won't probably"],"answer":"probably won't","explanation":"definitely / probably: after will, before won't.","explanation_ar":"مكان definitely وprobably."},{"q":"This time next week, we ___ on the beach in Jeddah.","options":["will be relaxing","relax","are relax","will relax"],"answer":"will be relaxing","explanation":"In progress at a future time → will be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل المستمر."},{"q":"Robots ___ replace all teachers. Students need people!","options":["won't definitely","definitely won't","definitely will not to","not will definitely"],"answer":"definitely won't","explanation":"definitely / probably: after will, before won't.","explanation_ar":"مكان definitely وprobably."},{"q":"My sister ___ study medicine – she hasn't decided yet.","options":["may to","will definitely","is going surely","may"],"answer":"may","explanation":"Possible, not sure → may / might (not) + base verb.","explanation_ar":"الاحتمال ← may/might."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with the future continuous. Word bank: will be watching, will be taking, will be living","items":[{"q":"At 7 p.m. tomorrow, I ______ (watch) the final with my cousins.","options":[],"answer":"will be watching","explanation":"In progress at a future time → will be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل المستمر."},{"q":"In 2050, people ______ (live) in smart homes.","options":[],"answer":"will be living","explanation":"In progress at a future time → will be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل المستمر."},{"q":"Don't call me at noon – I ______ (take) my piano exam.","options":[],"answer":"will be taking","explanation":"In progress at a future time → will be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل المستمر."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS1-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"Flying cars will to be common one day.","options":[],"answer":"Flying cars will be common one day.","explanation":"will to be → will be. will / may / might + base verb (no to, no -s).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: will to be → will be. المصدر بعد الأفعال الناقصة."},{"q":"My uncle might travels to Japan next year.","options":[],"answer":"My uncle might travel to Japan next year.","explanation":"might travels → might travel. will / may / might + base verb (no to, no -s).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: might travels → might travel. المصدر بعد الأفعال الناقصة."},{"q":"This time tomorrow, we will fly over the desert.","options":[],"answer":"This time tomorrow, we will be flying over the desert.","explanation":"will fly → will be flying. In progress at a future time → will be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: will fly → will be flying. المستقبل المستمر."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Make predictions about the future.","items":[{"q":"Something that will definitely happen in the next 20 years: ___","options":[],"answer":"Phones will definitely become smarter.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses predictions with will / won't (+ definitely, probably), may / might (not); the future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something that will probably happen: ___","options":[],"answer":"Most people will probably work from home sometimes.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses predictions with will / won't (+ definitely, probably), may / might (not); the future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something that might happen: ___","options":[],"answer":"People might take holidays in space.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses predictions with will / won't (+ definitely, probably), may / might (not); the future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something that probably won't happen: ___","options":[],"answer":"Robots probably won't play in the World Cup.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses predictions with will / won't (+ definitely, probably), may / might (not); the future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What you'll be doing at 8 p.m. tomorrow: ___","options":[],"answer":"At 8 p.m. tomorrow, I'll be doing my homework.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses predictions with will / won't (+ definitely, probably), may / might (not); the future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: My future timeline.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 predictions about life in 2050 with different certainty (definitely, probably, might).","options":[],"answer":"In 2050, cars will definitely be electric. People will probably use AI every day. Humans might live on the Moon.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses predictions with will / won't (+ definitely, probably), may / might (not); the future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about what you'll be doing in ten years (future continuous).","options":[],"answer":"In ten years, I'll be studying engineering. I'll be living in Riyadh.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses predictions with will / won't (+ definitely, probably), may / might (not); the future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one prediction you disagree with and say why.","options":[],"answer":"Some people say robots will replace doctors, but I think they won't because patients need human care.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses predictions with will / won't (+ definitely, probably), may / might (not); the future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spin & Speak","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Work in teams of four. Player 1 spins the wheel.","Make a correct sentence about the unit theme using the cue word and predictions with will / won't (+ definitely, probably), may / might (not); the future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time.","The team checks the sentence with the grammar box. Correct = 1 point; an extra detail = 1 bonus point.","Pass the spinner clockwise. Play for 6 minutes; the team with most points wins."],"data":[{"label":"will definitely"},{"label":"will probably"},{"label":"may"},{"label":"might"},{"label":"probably won't"},{"label":"definitely won't"},{"label":"This time next year, I'll be…"},{"label":"In 2050, people will be…"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"In the future, robots ___ do dangerous jobs.","options":["are will","will","wills","will to"],"answer":"will","explanation":"Sure prediction → will / won't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"تنبؤ مؤكد ← will."},{"q":"I'm not sure, but we ___ visit my grandmother this weekend.","options":["might","will definitely","are definitely","might to"],"answer":"might","explanation":"Possible, not sure → may / might (not) + base verb.","explanation_ar":"الاحتمال ← may/might."},{"q":"","options":["People won't probably use paper money in 2050.","People probably will not to use paper money in 2050.","People probably don't will use paper money in 2050.","People probably won't use paper money in 2050."],"answer":"People probably won't use paper money in 2050.","explanation":"definitely / probably: after will, before won't.","explanation_ar":"مكان definitely وprobably."},{"q":"At 10 o'clock tonight, I ___ my favorite program.","options":["will watch at","will be watching","watching will","am watch"],"answer":"will be watching","explanation":"In progress at a future time → will be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل المستمر."},{"q":"","options":["Doctors may use robots in most operations.","Doctors mays use robots in most operations.","Doctors may to use robots in most operations.","Doctors may uses robots in most operations."],"answer":"Doctors may use robots in most operations.","explanation":"will / may / might + base verb (no to, no -s).","explanation_ar":"المصدر بعد الأفعال الناقصة."},{"q":"Which sentence is the most certain?","options":["Electric cars may be cheaper.","Electric cars probably won't be cheaper.","Electric cars might be cheaper.","Electric cars will definitely be cheaper."],"answer":"Electric cars will definitely be cheaper.","explanation":"definitely / probably: after will, before won't.","explanation_ar":"مكان definitely وprobably."},{"q":"This time next month, my brother ___ his new job in Dammam.","options":["will started","will be starting","is start","starts at"],"answer":"will be starting","explanation":"In progress at a future time → will be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل المستمر."},{"q":"","options":["Robots don't definitely will feel emotions like humans.","Robots won't definitely feel emotions like humans.","Robots definitely won't feel emotions like humans.","Robots definitely will not to feel emotions like humans."],"answer":"Robots definitely won't feel emotions like humans.","explanation":"definitely / probably: after will, before won't.","explanation_ar":"مكان definitely وprobably."},{"q":"What ___ you be doing at noon on Friday?","options":["are","might to","will","do"],"answer":"will","explanation":"In progress at a future time → will be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل المستمر."},{"q":"There ___ be a test on Sunday – the teacher hasn't decided yet.","options":["may","may to","is surely","will definitely"],"answer":"may","explanation":"Possible, not sure → may / might (not) + base verb.","explanation_ar":"الاحتمال ← may/might."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Dr. Huda, a scientist in a white coat, speaking to a class on a video screen; behind her a futuristic Saudi city with solar towers, driverless taxis, delivery drones and a robot nurse; students holding prediction cards. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Dr. Huda, a scientist in a white coat, speaking to a class on a video screen; behind her a futuristic Saudi city with solar towers, driverless taxis, delivery drones and a robot nurse; students holding prediction cards"},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about predictions with will / won't (+ definitely, probably), may / might (not); the future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about predictions with will / won't (+ definitely, probably), may / might (not)"},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows predict (to say what you think will happen in the future); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing predict: to say what you think will happen in the future"},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows invention (a new thing that someone has made or designed); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing invention: a new thing that someone has made or designed"},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows device (a machine or tool made for a special job); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing device: a machine or tool made for a special job"},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows artificial (made by people, not natural); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing artificial: made by people, not natural"},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spin & Speak”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spin & Speak"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS1-W01","script":"predict. predict. Scientists predict hotter summers.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS1-W02","script":"invention. invention. The phone was an amazing invention.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS1-W03","script":"device. device. A smartwatch is a small device.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS1-W04","script":"artificial. artificial. Artificial intelligence can recognize faces.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS1-T1","script":"What will life be like in 2050? Our class asked a scientist, Dr. Huda, to share her predictions. \"In 2050, most cars will be electric, and many of them will drive themselves. Driverless taxis will probably be common in our cities. People may not need driving licenses at all!\" she says. \"Robots will definitely help in hospitals, and they might even cook our dinners. Artificial intelligence will be in almost every device we use.\" What about school? \"Students may study with virtual-reality headsets. In fact, this time next year, you'll be using apps that don't exist yet!\" Dr. Huda believes energy will be cleaner. \"By then, our country will be producing much of its electricity from the sun and the wind.\" Will people live on Mars? \"Possibly. A small colony might be living there, but most of us definitely won't move to space!\" Finally, she gave us some advice: \"The future isn't only something that happens to you. You'll be building it. So keep learning!\"","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Driverless Taxis Will Probably Be Common: will, may, might and the Future Continuous”. Let’s learn predictions with will / won't (+ definitely, probably), may / might (not); the future continuous (will be + -ing) for actions in progress at a future time together. Listen to the start of “Life in 2050”: What will life be like in 2050? Our class asked a scientist, Dr. Look at the green words. Use will / won't + base verb for predictions you feel sure about. Add definitely (very sure) or probably (quite sure) after will and before won't: Robots will definitely help in hospitals. People probably won't need keys. Use may or might + base verb when something is possible but not sure: Robots might cook our dinners. People may not need licenses. (may not / might not – no contraction mayn't.) Here are some examples. In twenty years, most homes will have solar panels. Doctors will probably use robots in operations. We might live in smart houses that talk to us. Be careful! Some learners say: “Robots will to cook our food.” That’s not right. We say: “Robots will cook our food.” will + base verb. Quick check: \"Robots might cook our dinners.\" Is the scientist sure? … Think! … No – it's only possible. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"Robots will probably help in hospitals, and they might cook our dinners.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS2","title":"I'm Meeting Him at Six: Choosing the Right Future Form","objectives":["Students will be able to choose between will, be going to, the present continuous and the present simple for the future.","Students will be able to explain the reason for each choice (decision, plan, arrangement, timetable, evidence).","I can say \"The train leaves at 6:15, and I'm meeting my cousin at the station.\"","I can say \"Look at those clouds – it's going to rain!\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من الاختيار بين will وbe going to والمضارع المستمر والمضارع البسيط للتعبير عن المستقبل.","سيتمكن الطلاب من شرح سبب كل اختيار (قرار، خطة، ترتيب، جدول، دليل).","أستطيع أن أقول The train leaves at 6:15, and I'm meeting my cousin at the station.","أستطيع أن أقول Look at those clouds – it's going to rain!"],"vocabulary":[{"word":"automatic","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˌɔtəˈmætɪk/","definition":"working by itself without a person","arabic":"آلي / تلقائي","example":"The doors are automatic.","image_id":"GV-L06-U2-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS2-W01"},{"word":"virtual","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈvɝtʃuəl/","definition":"made by a computer to look real","arabic":"افتراضي","example":"We visited a virtual museum online.","image_id":"GV-L06-U2-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS2-W02"},{"word":"sustainable","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/səˈsteɪnəbəl/","definition":"able to continue without harming the environment","arabic":"مستدام","example":"NEOM plans to be a sustainable city.","image_id":"GV-L06-U2-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS2-W03"},{"word":"population","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌpɑpjəˈleɪʃən/","definition":"the number of people who live in a place","arabic":"عدد السكان","example":"The world's population is over eight billion.","image_id":"GV-L06-U2-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"will – decisions made at the moment of speaking, offers and promises: The phone's ringing. I'll answer it! I'll help you. I won't tell anyone.\nbe going to – plans you decided before (intentions), and predictions based on evidence you can see now: I'm going to study robotics. Look at those clouds! It's going to rain.\nPresent continuous – fixed arrangements with other people (a time and place is agreed): I'm meeting Saad at six. Present simple – timetables and schedules: The train leaves at 6:15. The exam starts at 8.\nwill → instant decision, offer, promise, opinion-based prediction\nbe going to → plan/intention; prediction from present evidence\npresent continuous → personal arrangement (time + people)\npresent simple → timetable (trains, classes, films)","examples":["It's dark in here. – I'll switch on the light.","I'm going to save money for a new laptop.","Watch out! That glass is going to fall!","We're having dinner with our neighbors on Friday.","The new term starts on August 24.","I promise I won't forget your birthday.","Faisal is going to study computer science next year.","What time does the film begin?"],"common_errors":["✗ I'm tired. I'm going to sit down for a minute. (decided now) → ✓ I'm tired. I'll sit down for a minute. (Instant decision → will.)","✗ Look at the sky! It will rain. → ✓ Look at the sky! It's going to rain. (Evidence now → going to.)","✗ I meet my cousin tomorrow at six. → ✓ I'm meeting my cousin tomorrow at six. (Arrangement → present continuous.)","✗ The train is leaving at 6:15 every day. → ✓ The train leaves at 6:15 every day. (Timetable → present simple.)"],"arabic":"will للقرار في لحظة الكلام والعرض والوعد: I'll help you.\nbe going to للخطة المسبقة والتنبؤ بدليل حاضر: Look at those clouds! It's going to rain.\nالمضارع المستمر للترتيب المتفق عليه مع الآخرين: I'm meeting Saad at six.\nالمضارع البسيط للجداول والمواعيد الثابتة: The train leaves at 6:15."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “I'm Meeting Him at Six: Choosing the Right Future Form”. Let’s learn will (instant decisions, offers, promises, predictions), be going to (plans and evidence), present continuous (arrangements), present simple (timetables) together.","on_screen":"GV-L06-U2-LS2 | I'm Meeting Him at Six: Choosing the Right Future Form","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: I'll carry that. • We're going to paint the room. • I'm flying to Abha on Friday. • The flight lands at 9. I won't be late. • She isn't going to join. • We aren't meeting today. • The museum doesn't open until 10. Will you help me? • Are you going to enter the contest? • What are you doing tonight? • When does the bus leave?","on_screen":"I'll carry that. • We're going to paint the room. • I'm flying to Abha on Friday. • The flight lands at 9. | I won't be late. • She isn't going to join. • We aren't meeting today. • The museum doesn't open until 10. | Will you help me? • Are you going to enter the contest? • What are you doing tonight? • When does the bus leave?","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"will – decisions made at the moment of speaking, offers and promises: The phone's ringing. I'll answer it! I'll help you. I won't tell anyone. be going to – plans you decided before (intentions), and predictions based on evidence you can see now: I'm going to study robotics. Look at those clouds! It's going to rain.","on_screen":"will → instant decision, offer, promise, opinion-based prediction • be going to → plan/intention; prediction from present evidence • present continuous → personal arrangement (time + people)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. It's dark in here. – I'll switch on the light. I'm going to save money for a new laptop. Watch out! That glass is going to fall!","on_screen":"It's dark in here. – I'll switch on the light. / I'm going to save money for a new laptop. / Watch out! That glass is going to fall!","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I'm tired. I'm going to sit down for a minute. (decided now).” That’s not right. We say: “I'm tired. I'll sit down for a minute.” Instant decision → will.","on_screen":"✗ I'm tired. I'm going to sit down for a minute. (decided now)   ✓ I'm tired. I'll sit down for a minute.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"The phone's ringing. I'll answer it.\" Was this decided before? … Think! … No – just now. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"The train leaves at 6:15, and I'm meeting my cousin at the station.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"The train leaves at 6:15, and I'm meeting my cousin at the station.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: will (instant decisions, offers, promises, predictions), be going to (plans and evidence), present continuous (arrangements), present simple (timetables).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","will للقرار في لحظة الكلام والعرض والوعد: I'll help you.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I'm tired. I'm going to sit down for a minute. (decided now) — الصحيح: I'm tired. I'll sit down for a minute.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول The train leaves at 6:15, and I'm meeting my cousin at the station."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"\"This bag is heavy.\" – \"I ___ carry it for you.\"","options":["'m going to","carry","'m carrying","'ll"],"answer":"'ll","explanation":"Decision now, offer, promise → will.","explanation_ar":"القرار الآن ← will."},{"q":"We've already decided: we ___ visit Al-Ula in December.","options":["'ll be to","'re going to","'ll","visit"],"answer":"'re going to","explanation":"Plan or intention → be going to.","explanation_ar":"الخطة ← going to."},{"q":"Look at that boy on the wall! He ___ fall!","options":["'s going to","'s falling at","falls","'ll"],"answer":"'s going to","explanation":"Prediction from evidence now → be going to.","explanation_ar":"الدليل ← going to."},{"q":"I ___ the dentist at four tomorrow. It's in my calendar.","options":["'ll see","'m going see","'m seeing","see"],"answer":"'m seeing","explanation":"Arrangement with time/people → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"الترتيب ← المضارع المستمر."},{"q":"The school bus ___ at 6:45 every morning.","options":["leaves","'ll leave","'s going to leave","'s leaving"],"answer":"leaves","explanation":"Timetable → present simple.","explanation_ar":"الجدول ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"I promise I ___ tell anyone your secret.","options":["'m not telling","don't","'m not going to","won't"],"answer":"won't","explanation":"Decision now, offer, promise → will.","explanation_ar":"القرار الآن ← will."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS2-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the best future form. Word bank: is going to apply, are flying, opens","items":[{"q":"The science museum ______ (open) at 9 a.m. on weekdays.","options":[],"answer":"opens","explanation":"Timetable → present simple.","explanation_ar":"الجدول ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"My parents ______ (fly) to Istanbul on Saturday – they booked the tickets yesterday.","options":[],"answer":"are flying","explanation":"Arrangement with time/people → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"الترتيب ← المضارع المستمر."},{"q":"My cousin ______ (apply) to an engineering college – she made the decision months ago.","options":[],"answer":"is going to apply","explanation":"Plan or intention → be going to.","explanation_ar":"الخطة ← going to."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"Look at the smoke! The toast will burn!","options":[],"answer":"Look at the smoke! The toast is going to burn!","explanation":"will burn → is going to burn. Prediction from evidence now → be going to.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: will burn → is going to burn. الدليل ← going to."},{"q":"I meet Lina at the mall tomorrow at five.","options":[],"answer":"I am meeting Lina at the mall tomorrow at five.","explanation":"meet → am meeting. Arrangement with time/people → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: meet → am meeting. الترتيب ← المضارع المستمر."},{"q":"\"I'm cold.\" – \"Wait, I am going to close the window.\"","options":[],"answer":"\"I'm cold.\" – \"Wait, I 'll close the window.\"","explanation":"am going to close → 'll close. Decision now, offer, promise → will.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: am going to close → 'll close. القرار الآن ← will."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Talk about your future.","items":[{"q":"A plan you have for the holidays (going to): ___","options":[],"answer":"I'm going to learn to swim properly.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will (instant decisions, offers, promises, predictions), be going to (plans and evidence), present continuous (arrangements), present simple (timetables) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"An arrangement you have this week (present continuous): ___","options":[],"answer":"I'm visiting my grandparents on Friday.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will (instant decisions, offers, promises, predictions), be going to (plans and evidence), present continuous (arrangements), present simple (timetables) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A timetable fact (present simple): ___","options":[],"answer":"My first class starts at 7 a.m.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will (instant decisions, offers, promises, predictions), be going to (plans and evidence), present continuous (arrangements), present simple (timetables) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"An offer you can make to a friend (will): ___","options":[],"answer":"I'll help you with your math homework.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will (instant decisions, offers, promises, predictions), be going to (plans and evidence), present continuous (arrangements), present simple (timetables) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A prediction from evidence you can see now: ___","options":[],"answer":"The traffic is terrible. We're going to be late!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will (instant decisions, offers, promises, predictions), be going to (plans and evidence), present continuous (arrangements), present simple (timetables) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: My week ahead.","items":[{"q":"Write 2 arrangements and 1 timetable for next week.","options":[],"answer":"I'm playing football with my cousins on Thursday. I'm visiting the dentist on Sunday. The school trip leaves at 7:30 on Tuesday.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will (instant decisions, offers, promises, predictions), be going to (plans and evidence), present continuous (arrangements), present simple (timetables) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 plans for next year with going to.","options":[],"answer":"I'm going to join the robotics club. I'm going to read twenty books.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will (instant decisions, offers, promises, predictions), be going to (plans and evidence), present continuous (arrangements), present simple (timetables) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a mini-dialogue with an instant decision (will).","options":[],"answer":"\"We don't have any bread.\" – \"OK, I'll buy some on my way home.\"","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will (instant decisions, offers, promises, predictions), be going to (plans and evidence), present continuous (arrangements), present simple (timetables) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Tic-Tac-Grammar","mechanic":"tic_tac_toe","rules":["Two teams: X and O. Team X chooses a square.","Using the cue, the team says a correct sentence with will (instant decisions, offers, promises, predictions), be going to (plans and evidence), present continuous (arrangements), present simple (timetables) (the form in brackets: +, – or ?).","If the class and teacher agree it is correct, the team marks the square.","Three squares in a row wins. Play a second round with the grid turned around."],"data":[{"cue":"in 2050 / cars / definitely / be / electric"},{"cue":"robots / might / cook / our dinners"},{"cue":"people / probably / not / need / keys"},{"cue":"this time tomorrow / I / take / my exam"},{"cue":"at 8 p.m. / we / watch / the match"},{"cue":"in ten years / I / study / at university"},{"cue":"look at the clouds / it / rain"},{"cue":"the train / leave / at 6:15"},{"cue":"I / meet / my cousin / tomorrow evening"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"\"Someone's at the door.\" – \"I ___ get it.\"","options":["'m going to","get","'ll","'m getting"],"answer":"'ll","explanation":"Decision now, offer, promise → will.","explanation_ar":"القرار الآن ← will."},{"q":"She's saved a lot of money. She ___ buy a new laptop.","options":["'s going to","buys","'ll","'ll be to"],"answer":"'s going to","explanation":"Plan or intention → be going to.","explanation_ar":"الخطة ← going to."},{"q":"The sky is very dark. It ___ rain.","options":["'s going to","'s raining at","'ll","rains"],"answer":"'s going to","explanation":"Prediction from evidence now → be going to.","explanation_ar":"الدليل ← going to."},{"q":"","options":["We have a barbecue at our uncle's farm on Friday every week now.","We're having a barbecue at our uncle's farm on Friday.","We going to have a barbecue at our uncle's farm on Friday.","We'll have be a barbecue at our uncle's farm on Friday."],"answer":"We're having a barbecue at our uncle's farm on Friday.","explanation":"Arrangement with time/people → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"الترتيب ← المضارع المستمر."},{"q":"","options":["What time will start the match?","What time is the match start?","What time the match starts?","What time does the match start?"],"answer":"What time does the match start?","explanation":"Timetable → present simple.","explanation_ar":"الجدول ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"Which sentence shows a decision made right now?","options":["I'm making sandwiches at the party on Friday.","The sandwich shop opens at eight.","I'm hungry. I'll make a sandwich.","I'm going to make sandwiches for the trip next week."],"answer":"I'm hungry. I'll make a sandwich.","explanation":"Decision now, offer, promise → will.","explanation_ar":"القرار الآن ← will."},{"q":"","options":["I'm going meet my study group at the library at four.","I meet my study group at the library at four tomorrow.","I'm meeting my study group at the library at four.","I'll meeting my study group at the library at four."],"answer":"I'm meeting my study group at the library at four.","explanation":"Arrangement with time/people → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"الترتيب ← المضارع المستمر."},{"q":"The flight to Riyadh ___ at 10:40 p.m.","options":["is departing to","departs","will departing","departing"],"answer":"departs","explanation":"Timetable → present simple.","explanation_ar":"الجدول ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"Watch out! You ___ drop those plates!","options":["drop","'ll","'re dropping at","'re going to"],"answer":"'re going to","explanation":"Prediction from evidence now → be going to.","explanation_ar":"الدليل ← going to."},{"q":"Next year, my sister ___ study architecture. She has already applied.","options":["is going to","will maybe","studies","is study"],"answer":"is going to","explanation":"Plan or intention → be going to.","explanation_ar":"الخطة ← going to."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"Lina's phone screen showing a calendar with appointments, a train timetable on a station board, dark clouds outside a window, and Lina saying \"I'll help you!\" to her little brother who dropped his books. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Lina's phone screen showing a calendar with appointments, a train timetable on a station board, dark clouds outside a window, and Lina saying \"I'll help you!\" to her little brother who dropped his books"},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of will (instant decisions, offers, promises, predictions), be going to (plans and evidence), present continuous (arrangements), present simple (timetables): a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “The World of Tomorrow”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of will (instant decisions, offers, promises, predictions), be going to (plans and evidence), present continuous (arrangements), present simple (timetables): a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “The World of Tomorrow”"},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows automatic (working by itself without a person); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing automatic: working by itself without a person"},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows virtual (made by a computer to look real); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing virtual: made by a computer to look real"},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows sustainable (able to continue without harming the environment); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing sustainable: able to continue without harming the environment"},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows population (the number of people who live in a place); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing population: the number of people who live in a place"},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Tic-Tac-Grammar”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Tic-Tac-Grammar"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS2-W01","script":"automatic. automatic. The doors are automatic.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS2-W02","script":"virtual. virtual. We visited a virtual museum online.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS2-W03","script":"sustainable. sustainable. NEOM plans to be a sustainable city.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS2-W04","script":"population. population. The world's population is over eight billion.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “I'm Meeting Him at Six: Choosing the Right Future Form”. Let’s learn will (instant decisions, offers, promises, predictions), be going to (plans and evidence), present continuous (arrangements), present simple (timetables) together. Remember these patterns: I'll carry that. • We're going to paint the room. • I'm flying to Abha on Friday. • The flight lands at 9. I won't be late. • She isn't going to join. • We aren't meeting today. • The museum doesn't open until 10. Will you help me? • Are you going to enter the contest? • What are you doing tonight? • When does the bus leave? will – decisions made at the moment of speaking, offers and promises: The phone's ringing. I'll answer it! I'll help you. I won't tell anyone. be going to – plans you decided before (intentions), and predictions based on evidence you can see now: I'm going to study robotics. Look at those clouds! It's going to rain. Here are some examples. It's dark in here. – I'll switch on the light. I'm going to save money for a new laptop. Watch out! That glass is going to fall! Be careful! Some learners say: “I'm tired. I'm going to sit down for a minute. (decided now).” That’s not right. We say: “I'm tired. I'll sit down for a minute.” Instant decision → will. Quick check: \"The phone's ringing. I'll answer it.\" Was this decided before? … Think! … No – just now. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"The train leaves at 6:15, and I'm meeting my cousin at the station.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS3","title":"High-Tech, Eco-Friendly, World-Famous: Compound Adjectives","objectives":["Students will be able to understand and use common compound adjectives to describe technology and the future.","Students will be able to form compound adjectives such as a ten-year-old boy and a three-hour flight.","I can describe a device as \"user-friendly\" or \"energy-saving\".","I can say \"a three-hour flight\" (not \"three-hours\")."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من فهم الصفات المركبة الشائعة واستخدامها لوصف التكنولوجيا والمستقبل.","سيتمكن الطلاب من تكوين صفات مركبة مثل a ten-year-old boy وa three-hour flight.","أستطيع أن أصف جهازًا بأنه user-friendly أو energy-saving.","أستطيع أن أقول a three-hour flight (وليس three-hours)."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"possibility","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌpɑsəˈbɪləˌti/","definition":"something that might happen","arabic":"احتمال / إمكانية","example":"There's a possibility of rain tomorrow.","image_id":"GV-L06-U2-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS3-W01"},{"word":"innovation","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪnəˈveɪʃən/","definition":"a new idea or way of doing something","arabic":"ابتكار","example":"The app is a great innovation in education.","image_id":"GV-L06-U2-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS3-W02"},{"word":"colony","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkɑləni/","definition":"a group of people who live together in a new place","arabic":"مستعمرة / مستوطنة","example":"Scientists dream of a colony on Mars.","image_id":"GV-L06-U2-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS3-W03"},{"word":"replace","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˌriˈpleɪs/","definition":"to take the place of something","arabic":"يحلّ محلّ / يستبدل","example":"Robots may replace some workers.","image_id":"GV-L06-U2-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS3-W04"},{"word":"advanced","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ədˈvænst/","definition":"modern and developed","arabic":"متطوّر / متقدّم","example":"This is a very advanced robot.","image_id":"GV-L06-U2-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS3-W05"},{"word":"likely","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈlaɪkli/","definition":"probably going to happen","arabic":"مُرجَّح / محتمل","example":"It's likely that cars will fly one day.","image_id":"GV-L06-U2-LS3-W06","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS3-W06"}],"explanation":{"text":"A compound adjective is made of two (or more) words that work together to describe a noun: a high-tech phone, an eco-friendly bag. Before a noun, they are joined with a hyphen (-).\nCommon patterns: noun + -ing (energy-saving, time-saving, record-breaking); adjective/adverb + past participle (well-known, well-designed, solar-powered); adjective + noun (high-tech, long-distance, full-time); self- (self-driving, self-cleaning); -friendly (user-friendly, eco-friendly).\nWith number + noun, the noun is singular: a three-hour flight (NOT (not: three-hours)), a ten-year-old boy, a five-star hotel.\nCollocations/phrases: self-driving car • solar-powered house • energy-saving lamp • time-saving app | user-friendly website • eco-friendly bag • high-tech device • well-designed robot | world-famous inventor • record-breaking speed • long-lasting battery • ten-minute ride","examples":["My grandpa has a user-friendly phone with big buttons.","We bought an energy-saving air conditioner.","The museum has a self-driving bus.","Tesla's cars are world-famous.","This is a long-lasting battery – it works for two days.","We took a two-hour flight to Cairo.","She's a well-known scientist in the field of AI.","Paper straws are an eco-friendly choice."],"common_errors":["✗ It was a three-hours trip. → ✓ It was a three-hour trip. (number + noun → singular noun.)","✗ He is a ten years old boy. → ✓ He is a ten-year-old boy. (Hyphens + singular year.)","✗ This is a user friend app. → ✓ This is a user-friendly app. (-friendly.)","✗ The bus drives itself; it's a self-drive bus. → ✓ It's a self-driving bus. (self- + -ing.)"],"arabic":"الصفة المركبة كلمتان أو أكثر تصفان الاسم معًا، ونضع بينهما شرطة قبل الاسم: a high-tech phone.\nأنماط شائعة: اسم + ing (energy-saving)، well + التصريف الثالث (well-known)، self (self-driving)، friendly (user-friendly).\nمع الأرقام يكون الاسم مفردًا: a three-hour flight وa ten-year-old boy."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “High-Tech, Eco-Friendly, World-Famous: Compound Adjectives”. Let’s learn compound adjectives (adjective/noun + -ing participle, well + past participle, number + noun, self-/high-/user-); meaning and formation together.","on_screen":"GV-L06-U2-LS3 | High-Tech, Eco-Friendly, World-Famous: Compound Adjectives","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. possibility: something that might happen. innovation: a new idea or way of doing something. colony: a group of people who live together in a new place.","on_screen":"possibility | innovation | colony","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"A compound adjective is made of two (or more) words that work together to describe a noun: a high-tech phone, an eco-friendly bag. Before a noun, they are joined with a hyphen (-). Common patterns: noun + -ing (energy-saving, time-saving, record-breaking); adjective/adverb + past participle (well-known, well-designed, solar-powered); adjective + noun (high-tech, long-distance, full-time); self- (self-driving, self-cleaning); -friendly (user-friendly, eco-friendly).","on_screen":"compound adjectives (adjective/noun + -ing participle, well + past participle, number + noun, self-/high-/user-); meaning and formation","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. My grandpa has a user-friendly phone with big buttons. We bought an energy-saving air conditioner. The museum has a self-driving bus.","on_screen":"My grandpa has a user-friendly phone with big buttons. / We bought an energy-saving air conditioner. / The museum has a self-driving bus.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “It was a three-hours trip.” That’s not right. We say: “It was a three-hour trip.” number + noun → singular noun.","on_screen":"✗ It was a three-hours trip.   ✓ It was a three-hour trip.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"a three-hour flight\" – why not \"three-hours\"? … Think! … In compound adjectives, the noun is singular. Great job! Now you can say: I can describe a device as \"user-friendly\" or \"energy-saving\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can describe a device as \"user-friendly\" or \"energy-saving\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: compound adjectives (adjective/noun + -ing participle, well + past participle, number + noun, self-/high-/user-); meaning and formation.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الصفة المركبة كلمتان أو أكثر تصفان الاسم معًا، ونضع بينهما شرطة قبل الاسم: a high-tech phone.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: It was a three-hours trip. — الصحيح: It was a three-hour trip.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أصف جهازًا بأنه user-friendly أو energy-saving."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"This app is very ___ – even my grandmother can use it.","options":["user-friendly","using-friendly","user-friend","user-friendship"],"answer":"user-friendly","explanation":"Correct form (-ing / -ed / -friendly / self-).","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة."},{"q":"We stayed in a ___ hotel with a pool and a spa.","options":["five-stars","five-star","fifth-star","five-starred"],"answer":"five-star","explanation":"number + singular noun (a five-minute walk).","explanation_ar":"الرقم + اسم مفرد."},{"q":"The car doesn't need a driver. It's a ___ car.","options":["self-driving","self-driven it","self-drive","selfish-driving"],"answer":"self-driving","explanation":"Correct form (-ing / -ed / -friendly / self-).","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة."},{"q":"This lamp is ___; it uses very little electricity.","options":["saving-energy","energy-saved","energy-saving","energy-saves"],"answer":"energy-saving","explanation":"Choose the compound adjective with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"My brother is a ___ boy.","options":["twelve-year-olds","twelve years-old","twelve-years-old","twelve-year-old"],"answer":"twelve-year-old","explanation":"number + singular noun (a five-minute walk).","explanation_ar":"الرقم + اسم مفرد."},{"q":"The house uses only power from the sun. It's ___.","options":["solar-powering","power-solar","solar-powered","sun-powers"],"answer":"solar-powered","explanation":"Choose the compound adjective with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the compound adjective to its meaning.","items":[{"q":"eco-friendly","options":["using very modern technology","working or staying for a long time","not harmful to the environment","planned and made very well","known in every country","helping you do things faster"],"answer":"not harmful to the environment","explanation":"eco-friendly → not harmful to the environment. Choose the compound adjective with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"high-tech","options":["using very modern technology","working or staying for a long time","not harmful to the environment","planned and made very well","known in every country","helping you do things faster"],"answer":"using very modern technology","explanation":"high-tech → using very modern technology. Choose the compound adjective with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"world-famous","options":["using very modern technology","working or staying for a long time","not harmful to the environment","planned and made very well","known in every country","helping you do things faster"],"answer":"known in every country","explanation":"world-famous → known in every country. Choose the compound adjective with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"long-lasting","options":["using very modern technology","working or staying for a long time","not harmful to the environment","planned and made very well","known in every country","helping you do things faster"],"answer":"working or staying for a long time","explanation":"long-lasting → working or staying for a long time. Choose the compound adjective with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"time-saving","options":["using very modern technology","working or staying for a long time","not harmful to the environment","planned and made very well","known in every country","helping you do things faster"],"answer":"helping you do things faster","explanation":"time-saving → helping you do things faster. Choose the compound adjective with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"well-designed","options":["using very modern technology","working or staying for a long time","not harmful to the environment","planned and made very well","known in every country","helping you do things faster"],"answer":"planned and made very well","explanation":"well-designed → planned and made very well. Choose the compound adjective with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Describe things with compound adjectives.","items":[{"q":"Describe a device you use every day: ___","options":[],"answer":"My phone is a high-tech device with a long-lasting battery.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses compound adjectives (adjective/noun + -ing participle, well + past participle, number + noun, self-/high-/user-); meaning and formation correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Describe a journey you took (number + noun): ___","options":[],"answer":"I took a four-hour bus ride to Abha.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses compound adjectives (adjective/noun + -ing participle, well + past participle, number + noun, self-/high-/user-); meaning and formation correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Describe a famous person or place: ___","options":[],"answer":"The Kingdom Tower is a world-famous building.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses compound adjectives (adjective/noun + -ing participle, well + past participle, number + noun, self-/high-/user-); meaning and formation correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Describe an eco-friendly habit: ___","options":[],"answer":"Using a reusable bottle is an eco-friendly habit.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses compound adjectives (adjective/noun + -ing participle, well + past participle, number + noun, self-/high-/user-); meaning and formation correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Describe your dream invention: ___","options":[],"answer":"My dream invention is a self-cleaning bedroom!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses compound adjectives (adjective/noun + -ing participle, well + past participle, number + noun, self-/high-/user-); meaning and formation correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Design a gadget.","items":[{"q":"Invent a gadget for 2050. Describe it with 3 compound adjectives.","options":[],"answer":"My invention is a solar-powered, self-driving, user-friendly school bag that carries itself.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses compound adjectives (adjective/noun + -ing participle, well + past participle, number + noun, self-/high-/user-); meaning and formation correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences with number + noun compound adjectives.","options":[],"answer":"It has a twenty-hour battery. It's perfect for a ten-year-old student.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses compound adjectives (adjective/noun + -ing participle, well + past participle, number + noun, self-/high-/user-); meaning and formation correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one advertisement slogan with a compound adjective.","options":[],"answer":"Try the new eco-friendly bottle – good for you, good for the planet!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses compound adjectives (adjective/noun + -ing participle, well + past participle, number + noun, self-/high-/user-); meaning and formation correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Memory Match","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Place all cards face down in a grid.","Turn over two cards. If the word matches its definition, keep the pair and say a sentence with the word.","If not, turn them back over; the next player plays.","The player with the most pairs wins."],"data":[{"word":"predict","match":"to say what you think will happen in the future","arabic":"يتنبّأ"},{"word":"invention","match":"a new thing that someone has made or designed","arabic":"اختراع"},{"word":"device","match":"a machine or tool made for a special job","arabic":"جهاز"},{"word":"artificial","match":"made by people, not natural","arabic":"اصطناعي"},{"word":"automatic","match":"working by itself without a person","arabic":"آلي / تلقائي"},{"word":"virtual","match":"made by a computer to look real","arabic":"افتراضي"},{"word":"sustainable","match":"able to continue without harming the environment","arabic":"مستدام"},{"word":"population","match":"the number of people who live in a place","arabic":"عدد السكان"},{"word":"possibility","match":"something that might happen","arabic":"احتمال / إمكانية"},{"word":"innovation","match":"a new idea or way of doing something","arabic":"ابتكار"},{"word":"colony","match":"a group of people who live together in a new place","arabic":"مستعمرة / مستوطنة"},{"word":"replace","match":"to take the place of something","arabic":"يحلّ محلّ / يستبدل"},{"word":"advanced","match":"modern and developed","arabic":"متطوّر / متقدّم"},{"word":"likely","match":"probably going to happen","arabic":"مُرجَّح / محتمل"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The bags in this shop are ___ – they are made from recycled paper.","options":["eco-friendly","friendly-eco","eco-friend","eco-friendlier it"],"answer":"eco-friendly","explanation":"Correct form (-ing / -ed / -friendly / self-).","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة."},{"q":"It's a ___ walk from my house to the school.","options":["ten-minutes","tenth-minute","ten-minute","ten-minuted"],"answer":"ten-minute","explanation":"number + singular noun (a five-minute walk).","explanation_ar":"الرقم + اسم مفرد."},{"q":"Ibn Sina is a ___ doctor from history.","options":["well-knew","good-known","well-knowing","well-known"],"answer":"well-known","explanation":"Correct form (-ing / -ed / -friendly / self-).","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة."},{"q":"The new phone has a ___ battery that works for three days.","options":["long-lasted","lasting-long","long-lasting","long-lasts"],"answer":"long-lasting","explanation":"Choose the compound adjective with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"The runner ran at a ___ speed and won gold.","options":["breaking-record","record-breaks","record-breaking","record-broken"],"answer":"record-breaking","explanation":"Natural compound adjective + noun.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الطبيعية."},{"q":"","options":["My cousin works in a highly-tech company.","My cousin works in a high-techs company.","My cousin works in a tech-high company.","My cousin works in a high-tech company."],"answer":"My cousin works in a high-tech company.","explanation":"Natural compound adjective + noun.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الطبيعية."},{"q":"A website that is easy to use is ___.","options":["time-saving","world-famous","long-lasting","user-friendly"],"answer":"user-friendly","explanation":"Choose the compound adjective with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"","options":["We took a eight hours flight to Malaysia.","We took an eight-hour flight to Malaysia.","We took an eight-hours flight to Malaysia.","We took an eight-hour flights to Malaysia."],"answer":"We took an eight-hour flight to Malaysia.","explanation":"number + singular noun (a five-minute walk).","explanation_ar":"الرقم + اسم مفرد."},{"q":"Which one is a compound adjective?","options":["self-cleaning","clean","cleaner","cleaning"],"answer":"self-cleaning","explanation":"Correct form (-ing / -ed / -friendly / self-).","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة."},{"q":"This dishwasher is ___ – it saves you a lot of time.","options":["time-saved","time-saving","saving-time","time-saves"],"answer":"time-saving","explanation":"Choose the compound adjective with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A futuristic gadget expo: stands showing a solar-powered car, a self-driving bus, an energy-saving fridge, a user-friendly tablet for grandparents, and a world-famous robot shaking hands with visitors. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A futuristic gadget expo: stands showing a solar-powered car, a self-driving bus, an energy-saving fridge, a user-friendly tablet for grandparents, and a world-famous robot shaking hands with visitors"},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 6 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 6 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows possibility (something that might happen); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing possibility: something that might happen"},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows innovation (a new idea or way of doing something); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing innovation: a new idea or way of doing something"},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows colony (a group of people who live together in a new place); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing colony: a group of people who live together in a new place"},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows replace (to take the place of something); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing replace: to take the place of something"},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows advanced (modern and developed); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing advanced: modern and developed"},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS3-W06","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows likely (probably going to happen); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing likely: probably going to happen"},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Memory Match”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Memory Match"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS3-W01","script":"possibility. possibility. There's a possibility of rain tomorrow.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS3-W02","script":"innovation. innovation. The app is a great innovation in education.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS3-W03","script":"colony. colony. Scientists dream of a colony on Mars.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS3-W04","script":"replace. replace. Robots may replace some workers.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS3-W05","script":"advanced. advanced. This is a very advanced robot.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS3-W06","script":"likely. likely. It's likely that cars will fly one day.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “High-Tech, Eco-Friendly, World-Famous: Compound Adjectives”. Let’s learn compound adjectives (adjective/noun + -ing participle, well + past participle, number + noun, self-/high-/user-); meaning and formation together. Meet some new words. possibility: something that might happen. innovation: a new idea or way of doing something. colony: a group of people who live together in a new place. A compound adjective is made of two (or more) words that work together to describe a noun: a high-tech phone, an eco-friendly bag. Before a noun, they are joined with a hyphen (-). Common patterns: noun + -ing (energy-saving, time-saving, record-breaking); adjective/adverb + past participle (well-known, well-designed, solar-powered); adjective + noun (high-tech, long-distance, full-time); self- (self-driving, self-cleaning); -friendly (user-friendly, eco-friendly). Here are some examples. My grandpa has a user-friendly phone with big buttons. We bought an energy-saving air conditioner. The museum has a self-driving bus. Be careful! Some learners say: “It was a three-hours trip.” That’s not right. We say: “It was a three-hour trip.” number + noun → singular noun. Quick check: \"a three-hour flight\" – why not \"three-hours\"? … Think! … In compound adjectives, the noun is singular. Great job! Now you can say: I can describe a device as \"user-friendly\" or \"energy-saving\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS4","title":"A Well-Known Scientist Is Well Known: Hyphens in Compound Adjectives","objectives":["Students will be able to use hyphens in compound adjectives that come before a noun.","Students will be able to leave out hyphens after the verb be and after -ly adverbs, and hyphenate compound numbers.","I can write \"a well-known scientist\" and \"The scientist is well known.\"","I can write \"twenty-five\" and \"a highly advanced robot\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام الشرطة في الصفات المركبة التي تأتي قبل الاسم.","سيتمكن الطلاب من حذف الشرطة بعد فعل be وبعد الظروف المنتهية بـ -ly، ووضع الشرطة في الأعداد المركبة.","أستطيع أن أكتب a well-known scientist وThe scientist is well known.","أستطيع أن أكتب twenty-five وa highly advanced robot."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"predict","pos":"verb","ipa":"/prɪˈdɪkt/","definition":"to say what you think will happen in the future","arabic":"يتنبّأ","example":"Scientists predict hotter summers.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"invention","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈvɛnʃən/","definition":"a new thing that someone has made or designed","arabic":"اختراع","example":"The phone was an amazing invention.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"device","pos":"noun","ipa":"/dɪˈvaɪs/","definition":"a machine or tool made for a special job","arabic":"جهاز","example":"A smartwatch is a small device.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"artificial","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˌɑrtəˈfɪʃəl/","definition":"made by people, not natural","arabic":"اصطناعي","example":"Artificial intelligence can recognize faces.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"automatic","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˌɔtəˈmætɪk/","definition":"working by itself without a person","arabic":"آلي / تلقائي","example":"The doors are automatic.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"virtual","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈvɝtʃuəl/","definition":"made by a computer to look real","arabic":"افتراضي","example":"We visited a virtual museum online.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Use a hyphen when the compound adjective comes before the noun: a well-known scientist, a ten-year-old girl, an up-to-date map.\nWhen the compound comes after the verb be (or seem, become), we usually don't use a hyphen: The scientist is well known. The map is up to date. (Ages are an exception: She is ten years old – no hyphens, plural years.)\nSome compounds are always hyphenated because the dictionary lists them that way: eco-friendly, user-friendly, high-tech, world-famous (The bag is eco-friendly). Don't use a hyphen after an -ly adverb: a highly advanced robot, a carefully planned trip. Use hyphens in numbers from twenty-one to ninety-nine: twenty-one, forty-five, ninety-nine.\ncompound adjective + noun → hyphen: a long-distance runner\nbe + well/up-to compound → usually no hyphen: The book is well written. The map is up to date.\n-ly adverb + adjective → no hyphen: a fully charged phone\n21–99 → hyphen: thirty-two, sixty-seven","examples":["She's a well-known inventor.","The inventor is well known in Japan.","My brother is a twelve-year-old coder.","My brother is twelve years old.","We need an up-to-date map.","This is a highly advanced robot.","There are thirty-six students in the robotics club.","It was a carefully designed experiment."],"common_errors":["✗ She is a well known scientist. → ✓ She is a well-known scientist. (Before the noun → hyphen.)","✗ The book is well-written. → ✓ The book is well written. (After be → no hyphen.)","✗ It's a highly-advanced robot. → ✓ It's a highly advanced robot. (No hyphen after an -ly adverb.)","✗ There are twenty five students in my class. → ✓ There are twenty-five students in my class. (21–99 → hyphen.)"],"arabic":"نضع الشرطة في الصفة المركبة عندما تأتي قبل الاسم: a well-known scientist.\nبعد فعل be لا نضع الشرطة عادة: The scientist is well known. ومع العمر: He is ten years old.\nلا شرطة بعد الظرف المنتهي بـ ly: a highly advanced robot.\nنضع الشرطة في الأعداد من twenty-one إلى ninety-nine."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Well-Known Scientist Is Well Known: Hyphens in Compound Adjectives”. Let’s learn hyphens in compound adjectives before a noun; no hyphen after be; no hyphen after -ly adverbs; hyphens in numbers (twenty-one) and number + noun adjectives together.","on_screen":"GV-L06-U2-LS4 | A Well-Known Scientist Is Well Known: Hyphens in Compound Adjectives","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Use a hyphen when the compound adjective comes before the noun: a well-known scientist, a ten-year-old girl, an up-to-date map.","on_screen":"hyphens in compound adjectives before a noun; no hyphen after be; no hyphen after -ly adverbs; hyphens in numbers (twenty-one) and number + noun adjectives","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Use a hyphen when the compound adjective comes before the noun: a well-known scientist, a ten-year-old girl, an up-to-date map. When the compound comes after the verb be (or seem, become), we usually don't use a hyphen: The scientist is well known. The map is up to date. (Ages are an exception: She is ten years old – no hyphens, plural years.)","on_screen":"compound adjective + noun → hyphen: a long-distance runner • be + well/up-to compound → usually no hyphen: The book is well written. The map is up to date. • -ly adverb + adjective → no hyphen: a fully charged phone","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. She's a well-known inventor. The inventor is well known in Japan. My brother is a twelve-year-old coder.","on_screen":"She's a well-known inventor. / The inventor is well known in Japan. / My brother is a twelve-year-old coder.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “She is a well known scientist.” That’s not right. We say: “She is a well-known scientist.” Before the noun → hyphen.","on_screen":"✗ She is a well known scientist.   ✓ She is a well-known scientist.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"a ___ boy\" (ten year old) – hyphens? … Think! … Yes – *a ten-year-old boy*. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"a well-known scientist\" and \"The scientist is well known.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"a well-known scientist\" and \"The scientist is well known.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: hyphens in compound adjectives before a noun; no hyphen after be; no hyphen after -ly adverbs; hyphens in numbers (twenty-one) and number + noun adjectives.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نضع الشرطة في الصفة المركبة عندما تأتي قبل الاسم: a well-known scientist.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: She is a well known scientist. — الصحيح: She is a well-known scientist.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب a well-known scientist وThe scientist is well known."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"The New Falcon Phone (editing passage)","body":"Meet the Falcon X, a high tech phone for twenty first century students! It has a long lasting battery and a highly-sensitive camera. The phone is well-designed and easy to use. Order now and get a two year warranty!","word_count":39,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correctly punctuated sentence.","items":[{"q":"","options":["Ibn al-Haytham was a world famous-scientist.","Ibn al-Haytham was a-world-famous scientist.","Ibn al-Haytham was a world famous scientist-.","Ibn al-Haytham was a world-famous scientist."],"answer":"Ibn al-Haytham was a world-famous scientist.","explanation":"Compound adjective before a noun → hyphen.","explanation_ar":"قبل الاسم ← شرطة."},{"q":"","options":["His books are well known-around the world.","His books are well-known-around the world.","His books are well known around the world.","His books are-well known around the world."],"answer":"His books are well known around the world.","explanation":"After be → usually no hyphen.","explanation_ar":"بعد be ← بلا شرطة."},{"q":"","options":["It's a highly-intelligent robot.","It's a highly intelligent robot.","It's a highly intelligent-robot.","It's a-highly intelligent robot."],"answer":"It's a highly intelligent robot.","explanation":"-ly adverb + adjective → no hyphen.","explanation_ar":"بعد ly ← بلا شرطة."},{"q":"","options":["There are forty two countries in the competition.","There are forty-two countries in the competition.","There are forty two-countries in the competition.","There are forty-two-countries in the competition."],"answer":"There are forty-two countries in the competition.","explanation":"Numbers 21–99 → hyphen.","explanation_ar":"الأعداد ← شرطة."},{"q":"","options":["My sister is eight years old.","My sister is eight-year-old.","My sister is eight-years-old.","My sister is eight year-old."],"answer":"My sister is eight years old.","explanation":"a ten-year-old boy ↔ He is ten years old.","explanation_ar":"العمر."},{"q":"","options":["We watched a two hour-documentary about Mars.","We watched a two hour documentary about Mars.","We watched a two-hour documentary about Mars.","We watched a two-hours documentary about Mars."],"answer":"We watched a two-hour documentary about Mars.","explanation":"Compound adjective before a noun → hyphen.","explanation_ar":"قبل الاسم ← شرطة."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Add hyphens where needed. Write the phrase.","items":[{"q":"a solar powered car  (hyphen)","options":[],"answer":"a solar-powered car","explanation":"Compound adjective before a noun → hyphen.","explanation_ar":"قبل الاسم ← شرطة."},{"q":"The car is fully charged.  (no hyphen needed)","options":[],"answer":"The car is fully charged.","explanation":"-ly adverb + adjective → no hyphen.","explanation_ar":"بعد ly ← بلا شرطة."},{"q":"ninety nine robots  (hyphen)","options":[],"answer":"ninety-nine robots","explanation":"Numbers 21–99 → hyphen.","explanation_ar":"الأعداد ← شرطة."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS4-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"She has a ten year old brother.","options":[],"answer":"She has a ten-year-old brother.","explanation":"ten year old → ten-year-old. a ten-year-old boy ↔ He is ten years old.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: ten year old → ten-year-old. العمر."},{"q":"The website is up-to-date.","options":[],"answer":"The website is up to date.","explanation":"up-to-date → up to date. After be → usually no hyphen.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: up-to-date → up to date. بعد be ← بلا شرطة."},{"q":"It's a beautifully-designed phone.","options":[],"answer":"It's a beautifully designed phone.","explanation":"beautifully-designed → beautifully designed. -ly adverb + adjective → no hyphen.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: beautifully-designed → beautifully designed. بعد ly ← بلا شرطة."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the advertisement.","items":[{"q":"Meet the Falcon X, a high tech phone for twenty-first century students!","options":[],"answer":"Meet the Falcon X, a high-tech phone for twenty-first century students!","explanation":"high tech → high-tech. Compound adjective before a noun → hyphen.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: high tech → high-tech. قبل الاسم ← شرطة."},{"q":"Meet the Falcon X, a high-tech phone for twenty first century students!","options":[],"answer":"Meet the Falcon X, a high-tech phone for twenty-first century students!","explanation":"twenty first → twenty-first. Compound adjective before a noun → hyphen.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: twenty first → twenty-first. قبل الاسم ← شرطة."},{"q":"It has a long lasting battery and a highly sensitive camera.","options":[],"answer":"It has a long-lasting battery and a highly sensitive camera.","explanation":"long lasting → long-lasting. Compound adjective before a noun → hyphen.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: long lasting → long-lasting. قبل الاسم ← شرطة."},{"q":"It has a long-lasting battery and a highly-sensitive camera.","options":[],"answer":"It has a long-lasting battery and a highly sensitive camera.","explanation":"highly-sensitive → highly sensitive. Compound adjective before a noun → hyphen.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: highly-sensitive → highly sensitive. قبل الاسم ← شرطة."},{"q":"The phone is well-designed and easy to use.","options":[],"answer":"The phone is well designed and easy to use.","explanation":"well-designed → well designed. Compound adjective before a noun → hyphen.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: well-designed → well designed. قبل الاسم ← شرطة."},{"q":"Order now and get a two year warranty!","options":[],"answer":"Order now and get a two-year warranty!","explanation":"two year → two-year. Compound adjective before a noun → hyphen.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: two year → two-year. قبل الاسم ← شرطة."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write with hyphens.","items":[{"q":"Write 2 sentences with the same compound: one before a noun, one after be.","options":[],"answer":"It's a well-written article. The article is well written.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses hyphens in compound adjectives before a noun; no hyphen after be; no hyphen after -ly adverbs; hyphens in numbers (twenty-one) and number + noun adjectives correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your age in two ways.","options":[],"answer":"I'm a thirteen-year-old student. I'm thirteen years old.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses hyphens in compound adjectives before a noun; no hyphen after be; no hyphen after -ly adverbs; hyphens in numbers (twenty-one) and number + noun adjectives correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with an -ly adverb + adjective and one with a number from 21 to 99.","options":[],"answer":"We visited a newly opened museum. It has fifty-four rooms.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses hyphens in compound adjectives before a noun; no hyphen after be; no hyphen after -ly adverbs; hyphens in numbers (twenty-one) and number + noun adjectives correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Builder","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["The teacher reads a word and a short clue.","Teams build the word with letter tiles in 30 seconds.","The team holds up the word; correct spelling = 1 point, with correct capital letter or punctuation where needed = 1 bonus point.","Continue until all words are used."],"data":[{"word":"invention","clue":"a new thing that someone has made or designed"},{"word":"artificial","clue":"made by people, not natural"},{"word":"sustainable","clue":"able to continue without harming the environment"},{"word":"population","clue":"the number of people who live in a place"},{"word":"possibility","clue":"something that might happen"},{"word":"innovation","clue":"a new idea or way of doing something"},{"word":"predict","clue":"to say what you think will happen in the future"},{"word":"device","clue":"a machine or tool made for a special job"},{"word":"automatic","clue":"working by itself without a person"},{"word":"virtual","clue":"made by a computer to look real"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["We bought an-energy saving fridge.","We bought an energy-saving fridge.","We bought an energy-saving-fridge.","We bought an energy saving-fridge."],"answer":"We bought an energy-saving fridge.","explanation":"Compound adjective before a noun → hyphen.","explanation_ar":"قبل الاسم ← شرطة."},{"q":"","options":["The information on this website is up to-date.","The information on this website is up-to date.","The information on this-website is up to date.","The information on this website is up to date."],"answer":"The information on this website is up to date.","explanation":"After be → usually no hyphen.","explanation_ar":"بعد be ← بلا شرطة."},{"q":"","options":["She wrote a carefully researched report.","She wrote a carefully researched-report.","She wrote a-carefully researched report.","She wrote a carefully-researched report."],"answer":"She wrote a carefully researched report.","explanation":"-ly adverb + adjective → no hyphen.","explanation_ar":"بعد ly ← بلا شرطة."},{"q":"How do we write 63 in words?","options":["six-ty three","sixty-three","sixty three","sixtythree"],"answer":"sixty-three","explanation":"Numbers 21–99 → hyphen.","explanation_ar":"الأعداد ← شرطة."},{"q":"","options":["My cousin is a fifteen-year old-programmer.","My cousin is a fifteen-year-old programmer.","My cousin is a fifteen-years-old programmer.","My cousin is a fifteen year old programmer."],"answer":"My cousin is a fifteen-year-old programmer.","explanation":"a ten-year-old boy ↔ He is ten years old.","explanation_ar":"العمر."},{"q":"Which phrase needs a hyphen?","options":["the app is well known","a fully charged tablet","a newly built road","a well known app"],"answer":"a well known app","explanation":"Compound adjective before a noun → hyphen.","explanation_ar":"قبل الاسم ← شرطة."},{"q":"","options":["Our teacher is very well-organized-.","Our teacher is very-well organized.","Our teacher is very well organized.","Our teacher is-very well organized."],"answer":"Our teacher is very well organized.","explanation":"After be → usually no hyphen.","explanation_ar":"بعد be ← بلا شرطة."},{"q":"","options":["The city has a-brand new metro system.","The city has a brand-new-metro system.","The city has a brand-new metro system.","The city has a brand new-metro system."],"answer":"The city has a brand-new metro system.","explanation":"Compound adjective before a noun → hyphen.","explanation_ar":"قبل الاسم ← شرطة."},{"q":"Which phrase is punctuated correctly?","options":["a-newly discovered planet","a newly-discovered planet","a newly discovered-planet","a newly discovered planet"],"answer":"a newly discovered planet","explanation":"-ly adverb + adjective → no hyphen.","explanation_ar":"بعد ly ← بلا شرطة."},{"q":"","options":["Thirty-one students joined the coding club.","Thirty-one-students joined the coding club.","Thirty one students joined the coding club.","Thirtyone students joined the coding club."],"answer":"Thirty-one students joined the coding club.","explanation":"Numbers 21–99 → hyphen.","explanation_ar":"الأعداد ← شرطة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “The World of Tomorrow” that shows hyphens in compound adjectives before a noun; no hyphen after be; no hyphen after -ly adverbs; hyphens in numbers (twenty-one) and number + noun adjectives in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “The World of Tomorrow” that shows hyphens in compound adjectives before a noun; no hyphen after be; no hyphen after -ly adverbs; hyphens in numbers (twenty-one) and number + noun adjectives in action"},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Builder”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Builder"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Well-Known Scientist Is Well Known: Hyphens in Compound Adjectives”. Let’s learn hyphens in compound adjectives before a noun; no hyphen after be; no hyphen after -ly adverbs; hyphens in numbers (twenty-one) and number + noun adjectives together. Use a hyphen when the compound adjective comes before the noun: a well-known scientist, a ten-year-old girl, an up-to-date map. Use a hyphen when the compound adjective comes before the noun: a well-known scientist, a ten-year-old girl, an up-to-date map. When the compound comes after the verb be (or seem, become), we usually don't use a hyphen: The scientist is well known. The map is up to date. (Ages are an exception: She is ten years old – no hyphens, plural years.) Here are some examples. She's a well-known inventor. The inventor is well known in Japan. My brother is a twelve-year-old coder. Be careful! Some learners say: “She is a well known scientist.” That’s not right. We say: “She is a well-known scientist.” Before the noun → hyphen. Quick check: \"a ___ boy\" (ten year old) – hyphens? … Think! … Yes – *a ten-year-old boy*. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"a well-known scientist\" and \"The scientist is well known.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS5","title":"Our School in 2050: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to present predictions and plans for the future of their school.","Students will be able to write a vision text with future forms and correctly hyphenated compound adjectives.","I can present my vision of the school of the future.","I can write about the future with the right future forms."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تقديم تنبؤات وخطط لمستقبل مدرستهم.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة نص رؤية بصيغ المستقبل وصفات مركبة صحيحة الترقيم.","أستطيع أن أقدّم رؤيتي لمدرسة المستقبل.","أستطيع أن أكتب عن المستقبل بصيغ المستقبل الصحيحة."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"predict","pos":"verb","ipa":"/prɪˈdɪkt/","definition":"to say what you think will happen in the future","arabic":"يتنبّأ","example":"Scientists predict hotter summers.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"invention","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈvɛnʃən/","definition":"a new thing that someone has made or designed","arabic":"اختراع","example":"The phone was an amazing invention.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"device","pos":"noun","ipa":"/dɪˈvaɪs/","definition":"a machine or tool made for a special job","arabic":"جهاز","example":"A smartwatch is a small device.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"artificial","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˌɑrtəˈfɪʃəl/","definition":"made by people, not natural","arabic":"اصطناعي","example":"Artificial intelligence can recognize faces.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"automatic","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˌɔtəˈmætɪk/","definition":"working by itself without a person","arabic":"آلي / تلقائي","example":"The doors are automatic.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"virtual","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈvɝtʃuəl/","definition":"made by a computer to look real","arabic":"افتراضي","example":"We visited a virtual museum online.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"sustainable","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/səˈsteɪnəbəl/","definition":"able to continue without harming the environment","arabic":"مستدام","example":"NEOM plans to be a sustainable city.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"population","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌpɑpjəˈleɪʃən/","definition":"the number of people who live in a place","arabic":"عدد السكان","example":"The world's population is over eight billion.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"possibility","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌpɑsəˈbɪləˌti/","definition":"something that might happen","arabic":"احتمال / إمكانية","example":"There's a possibility of rain tomorrow.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"innovation","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪnəˈveɪʃən/","definition":"a new idea or way of doing something","arabic":"ابتكار","example":"The app is a great innovation in education.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"colony","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkɑləni/","definition":"a group of people who live together in a new place","arabic":"مستعمرة / مستوطنة","example":"Scientists dream of a colony on Mars.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"replace","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˌriˈpleɪs/","definition":"to take the place of something","arabic":"يحلّ محلّ / يستبدل","example":"Robots may replace some workers.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"advanced","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ədˈvænst/","definition":"modern and developed","arabic":"متطوّر / متقدّم","example":"This is a very advanced robot.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"likely","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈlaɪkli/","definition":"probably going to happen","arabic":"مُرجَّح / محتمل","example":"It's likely that cars will fly one day.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 2: will / may / might, the future continuous, the four future forms, and compound adjectives with correct hyphens.\nA vision text makes predictions (will definitely, might), describes scenes in progress (students will be studying), and adds plans (we're going to…).\n✔ will definitely / probably • may / might (not)\n✔ will be + -ing (in progress at a future time)\n✔ going to (plan) • present continuous (arrangement) • present simple (timetable)\n✔ a well-designed school ↔ The school is well designed.","examples":["In 2050, schools will probably have robot assistants.","Students might learn from home two days a week.","At noon, students will be eating food from the school garden.","We're going to present our model on Thursday.","The science fair opens at 9 a.m.","It will be an eco-friendly building.","The building will be well designed and quiet.","The classrooms will have high-tech screens."],"common_errors":["✗ In 2050, students will studying online. → ✓ In 2050, students will be studying online. (will be + -ing.)","✗ Our group will build a model for the fair. (it's a plan) → ✓ Our group is going to build a model for the fair. (Plan → going to.)","✗ It will be a solar powered school. → ✓ It will be a solar-powered school. (Before the noun → hyphen.)"],"arabic":"نراجع will وmay وmight والمستقبل المستمر وصيغ المستقبل الأربع والصفات المركبة والشرطة.\nنص الرؤية يحتوي على تنبؤات ومشاهد جارية في المستقبل وخطط.\nتذكّر: شرطة قبل الاسم، ولا شرطة بعد be أو بعد ly."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Our School in 2050: Language in Use”. Let’s learn will / may / might, future continuous, future forms contrast, compound adjectives and hyphens (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L06-U2-LS5 | Our School in 2050: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Future school expo: in groups, design the school of 2050. Present 2 predictions (will definitely / might), one future-continuous sentence (In 2050, students will be…), one plan (We're going to…), and 3 compound adjectives. The class votes for the best design.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 2: will / may / might, the future continuous, the four future forms, and compound adjectives with correct hyphens. A vision text makes predictions (will definitely, might), describes scenes in progress (students will be studying), and adds plans (we're going to…).","on_screen":"✔ will definitely / probably • may / might (not) • ✔ will be + -ing (in progress at a future time) • ✔ going to (plan) • present continuous (arrangement) • present simple (timetable)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. In 2050, schools will probably have robot assistants. Students might learn from home two days a week. At noon, students will be eating food from the school garden.","on_screen":"In 2050, schools will probably have robot assistants. / Students might learn from home two days a week. / At noon, students will be eating food from the school garden.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “In 2050, students will studying online.” That’s not right. We say: “In 2050, students will be studying online.” will be + -ing.","on_screen":"✗ In 2050, students will studying online.   ✓ In 2050, students will be studying online.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “Our group will build a model for the fair. (it's a plan)”? … Think! … It should be “Our group is going to build a model for the fair.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can present my vision of the school of the future.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can present my vision of the school of the future.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: will / may / might, future continuous, future forms contrast, compound adjectives and hyphens (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع will وmay وmight والمستقبل المستمر وصيغ المستقبل الأربع والصفات المركبة والشرطة.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: In 2050, students will studying online. — الصحيح: In 2050, students will be studying online.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقدّم رؤيتي لمدرسة المستقبل."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Our School in 2050 – Group 3","body":"In 2050, our school will definitely be solar-powered, and it will probably produce more energy than it uses.\nStudents might not carry heavy bags, because all their books will be on lightweight tablets.\nEvery morning, a self-driving bus will collect students, and it will be completely silent.\nAt 10 a.m., students will be studying in virtual-reality labs; they might visit ancient Rome or the surface of Mars!\nThe school library will be run by a user-friendly robot that knows every book.\nBut teachers definitely won't disappear – students will always need real people to guide them.\nOur group is going to build a model of this school for the science fair, which starts on March 3.","word_count":116,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read \"Our School in 2050\". True or False?","items":[{"q":"The school will definitely be solar-powered.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Our School in 2050 – Group 3”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Students will carry heavy bags full of books.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Our School in 2050 – Group 3”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"A self-driving bus will collect the students.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Our School in 2050 – Group 3”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"At 10 a.m., students will be studying in virtual-reality labs.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Our School in 2050 – Group 3”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Group 3 thinks teachers will disappear.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Our School in 2050 – Group 3”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The science fair starts on March 3.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Our School in 2050 – Group 3”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"In 2050, the school will ___ be solar-powered.","options":["defining","definite","define","definitely"],"answer":"definitely","explanation":"will / may / might predictions.","explanation_ar":"التنبؤ."},{"q":"Students ___ not carry heavy bags.","options":["will to","might","might to","are"],"answer":"might","explanation":"will / may / might predictions.","explanation_ar":"التنبؤ."},{"q":"At 10 a.m., students will ___ in virtual-reality labs.","options":["study at","studying","be studying","be study"],"answer":"be studying","explanation":"Future continuous.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل المستمر."},{"q":"Our group ___ build a model for the science fair.","options":["is going to","builds","will maybe","is build"],"answer":"is going to","explanation":"Choosing the right future form.","explanation_ar":"صيغة المستقبل."},{"q":"The science fair ___ on March 3.","options":["is starting to","starts","start","will starting"],"answer":"starts","explanation":"Choosing the right future form.","explanation_ar":"صيغة المستقبل."},{"q":"","options":["The library will be run by a user-friendly-robot.","The library will be run by an user-friendly robot.","The library will be run by a user-friendly robot.","The library will be run by a user friendly robot."],"answer":"The library will be run by a user-friendly robot.","explanation":"Compound adjective and hyphen.","explanation_ar":"الصفة المركبة."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Plan your future school expo.","items":[{"q":"Prediction 1 (will definitely / probably): ___","options":[],"answer":"Our school will definitely have a rooftop garden.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will / may / might, future continuous, future forms contrast, compound adjectives and hyphens (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Prediction 2 (may / might): ___","options":[],"answer":"Students might study with robot tutors.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will / may / might, future continuous, future forms contrast, compound adjectives and hyphens (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A scene in progress (In 2050, students will be…): ___","options":[],"answer":"In 2050, students will be growing their own vegetables.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will / may / might, future continuous, future forms contrast, compound adjectives and hyphens (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Your group's plan (going to): ___","options":[],"answer":"We're going to make a model from recycled boxes.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will / may / might, future continuous, future forms contrast, compound adjectives and hyphens (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"3 compound adjectives for your school: ___","options":[],"answer":"eco-friendly, high-tech, well-designed","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will / may / might, future continuous, future forms contrast, compound adjectives and hyphens (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write \"My School in 2050\".","items":[{"q":"Plan: 2 predictions, 1 future-continuous scene, 1 plan, 1 timetable, 3 compound adjectives.","options":[],"answer":"definitely: a solar-powered roof; might: robot teachers' assistants; scene: students will be flying drones in science; plan: going to present at assembly; timetable: assembly starts at 7:15; eco-friendly, high-tech, world-famous","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will / may / might, future continuous, future forms contrast, compound adjectives and hyphens (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your text in 7–8 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"In 2050, my school will definitely have a solar-powered roof. Robots might help the teachers in class. In science lessons, students will be flying drones over the school. The playground will be eco-friendly, with trees everywhere. The labs will be high-tech and well designed. Our school might become world-famous! We're going to present our ideas at the assembly, which starts at 7:15 on Sunday.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will / may / might, future continuous, future forms contrast, compound adjectives and hyphens (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: future forms? will be + -ing? hyphens? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"a well designed lab\" to \"a well-designed lab\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will / may / might, future continuous, future forms contrast, compound adjectives and hyphens (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Quiz Show Challenge","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Teams take turns choosing a category and a cue word.","Grammar: make a sentence with will / may / might, future continuous, future forms contrast, compound adjectives and hyphens (unit review). Words: give the meaning. Spelling: spell it. Write It!: write a sentence with correct punctuation.","Correct answers score 10 points; teams may steal a question another team misses.","The highest score after 8 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"predict","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"invention","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"device","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"artificial","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"automatic","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"virtual","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"sustainable","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"population","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"possibility","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"innovation","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"colony","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"replace","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"advanced","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"likely","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"People ___ live much longer in the future.","options":["will probably","probably will to","probably will be to","will probable"],"answer":"will probably","explanation":"will / may / might predictions.","explanation_ar":"التنبؤ."},{"q":"","options":["Cars may not need drivers in 2050.","Cars may not to need drivers in 2050.","Cars mayn't need drivers in 2050.","Cars may not needs drivers in 2050."],"answer":"Cars may not need drivers in 2050.","explanation":"will / may / might predictions.","explanation_ar":"التنبؤ."},{"q":"This time tomorrow, I ___ on a plane to Jeddah.","options":["am sit","sitting will","will be sitting","will sit at"],"answer":"will be sitting","explanation":"Future continuous.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل المستمر."},{"q":"\"I've lost my pen.\" – \"Don't worry, I ___ lend you one.\"","options":["'m lending","'m going to","'ll","lend"],"answer":"'ll","explanation":"Choosing the right future form.","explanation_ar":"صيغة المستقبل."},{"q":"My brother ___ his friends at the stadium at 7 p.m. – it's all arranged.","options":["meet","is meeting","meets every","will meeting"],"answer":"is meeting","explanation":"Choosing the right future form.","explanation_ar":"صيغة المستقبل."},{"q":"Look at that robot! It ___ crash into the wall!","options":["'ll","crashes","'s crashing at","'s going to"],"answer":"'s going to","explanation":"Choosing the right future form.","explanation_ar":"صيغة المستقبل."},{"q":"","options":["The robot is very well-designed-.","The robot is very well designed.","The robot is very well designs.","The robot is very-well designed."],"answer":"The robot is very well designed.","explanation":"Compound adjective and hyphen.","explanation_ar":"الصفة المركبة."},{"q":"","options":["We'll take a six-hours flight to London.","We'll take a six-hour flight to London.","We'll take a six hours flight to London.","We'll take a six-hour-flight to London."],"answer":"We'll take a six-hour flight to London.","explanation":"Compound adjective and hyphen.","explanation_ar":"الصفة المركبة."},{"q":"The school bus ___ at 6:30 tomorrow, so don't be late.","options":["is leave","will leaving","leaving","leaves"],"answer":"leaves","explanation":"Choosing the right future form.","explanation_ar":"صيغة المستقبل."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for a vision of the future:","options":["In 2050, students will learning in eco friendly classrooms, and robots might helps them.","In 2050, students will be learn in eco-friendly-classrooms, and robots help them.","In 2050, students are learn in eco-friendly classrooms, and robots might to help them.","In 2050, students will be learning in eco-friendly classrooms, and robots might help them."],"answer":"In 2050, students will be learning in eco-friendly classrooms, and robots might help them.","explanation":"Future continuous.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل المستمر."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"A model of a futuristic school made from recycled materials: solar panels on the roof, a robot librarian, VR headsets on desks, a vertical garden, and students presenting it to Ms. Huda. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A model of a futuristic school made from recycled materials: solar panels on the roof, a robot librarian, VR headsets on desks, a vertical garden, and students presenting it to Ms. Huda"},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “The World of Tomorrow”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “The World of Tomorrow”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L06-U2-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Quiz Show Challenge”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Quiz Show Challenge"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS5-T1","script":"In 2050, our school will definitely be solar-powered, and it will probably produce more energy than it uses. Students might not carry heavy bags, because all their books will be on lightweight tablets. Every morning, a self-driving bus will collect students, and it will be completely silent. At 10 a.m., students will be studying in virtual-reality labs; they might visit ancient Rome or the surface of Mars! The school library will be run by a user-friendly robot that knows every book. But teachers definitely won't disappear – students will always need real people to guide them. Our group is going to build a model of this school for the science fair, which starts on March 3.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U2-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Our School in 2050: Language in Use”. Let’s learn will / may / might, future continuous, future forms contrast, compound adjectives and hyphens (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Future school expo: in groups, design the school of 2050. Present 2 predictions (will definitely / might), one future-continuous sentence (In 2050, students will be…), one plan (We're going to…), and 3 compound adjectives. The class votes for the best design. Today you use all of Unit 2: will / may / might, the future continuous, the four future forms, and compound adjectives with correct hyphens. A vision text makes predictions (will definitely, might), describes scenes in progress (students will be studying), and adds plans (we're going to…). Here are some examples. In 2050, schools will probably have robot assistants. Students might learn from home two days a week. At noon, students will be eating food from the school garden. Be careful! Some learners say: “In 2050, students will studying online.” That’s not right. We say: “In 2050, students will be studying online.” will be + -ing. Quick check: what is wrong with “Our group will build a model for the fair. (it's a plan)”? … Think! … It should be “Our group is going to build a model for the fair.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can present my vision of the school of the future.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"In the future, most phones ___ fold like paper.","options":["will","are will","wills","will to"],"answer":"will","explanation":"Sure prediction → will / won't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"تنبؤ مؤكد ← will."},{"q":"I'm not sure, but I ___ join the coding club next term.","options":["will definitely","may to","may","am definitely"],"answer":"may","explanation":"Possible, not sure → may / might (not) + base verb.","explanation_ar":"الاحتمال ← may/might."},{"q":"","options":["Robots won't probably replace nurses.","Robots probably don't will replace nurses.","Robots probably won't replace nurses.","Robots probably will not to replace nurses."],"answer":"Robots probably won't replace nurses.","explanation":"definitely / probably: after will, before won't.","explanation_ar":"مكان definitely وprobably."},{"q":"At 9 p.m. tonight, my family ___ dinner at my uncle's house.","options":["are have","having will","will have at","will be having"],"answer":"will be having","explanation":"In progress at a future time → will be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل المستمر."},{"q":"","options":["Scientists might finds life on another planet.","Scientists might to find life on another planet.","Scientists mights find life on another planet.","Scientists might find life on another planet."],"answer":"Scientists might find life on another planet.","explanation":"will / may / might + base verb (no to, no -s).","explanation_ar":"المصدر بعد الأفعال الناقصة."},{"q":"\"The printer isn't working.\" – \"I ___ call the technician.\"","options":["call","'ll","'m going to","'m calling"],"answer":"'ll","explanation":"Decision now, offer, promise → will.","explanation_ar":"القرار الآن ← will."},{"q":"We've saved enough money. We ___ buy a 3D printer for the club.","options":["buy","'ll be to","'re going to","'ll"],"answer":"'re going to","explanation":"Plan or intention → be going to.","explanation_ar":"الخطة ← going to."},{"q":"Look at the ice on the road! Someone ___ slip!","options":["'s going to","slips","'ll","'s slipping at"],"answer":"'s going to","explanation":"Prediction from evidence now → be going to.","explanation_ar":"الدليل ← going to."},{"q":"","options":["I'm having lunch with my grandparents on Friday.","I going to have lunch with my grandparents on Friday.","I have lunch with my grandparents on Friday every week now.","I'll having lunch with my grandparents on Friday."],"answer":"I'm having lunch with my grandparents on Friday.","explanation":"Arrangement with time/people → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"الترتيب ← المضارع المستمر."},{"q":"The robotics competition ___ at 8 a.m. on Saturday.","options":["is beginning to","begins","will beginning","begin"],"answer":"begins","explanation":"Timetable → present simple.","explanation_ar":"الجدول ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"My little brother is a ___ boy.","options":["nine-year-olds","nine years-old","nine-year-old","nine-years-old"],"answer":"nine-year-old","explanation":"number + singular noun (a five-minute walk).","explanation_ar":"الرقم + اسم مفرد."},{"q":"The new metro is fast and ___ – it doesn't pollute the air.","options":["eco-friendlier it","eco-friendly","friendly-eco","eco-friend"],"answer":"eco-friendly","explanation":"Correct form (-ing / -ed / -friendly / self-).","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة."},{"q":"Al-Khwarizmi was a ___ mathematician.","options":["famous-world","world-fame","world-famed-of","world-famous"],"answer":"world-famous","explanation":"Choose the compound adjective with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"A battery that works for a long time is ___.","options":["time-saving","long-lasting","high-tech","user-friendly"],"answer":"long-lasting","explanation":"Choose the compound adjective with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"","options":["We watched a three-hour film about space.","We watched a three-hours film about space.","We watched a three-hour-film about space.","We watched a three hours film about space."],"answer":"We watched a three-hour film about space.","explanation":"number + singular noun (a five-minute walk).","explanation_ar":"الرقم + اسم مفرد."},{"q":"","options":["Al-Biruni is a well-known-scholar.","Al-Biruni is a well-known scholar.","Al-Biruni is a-well known scholar.","Al-Biruni is a well known-scholar."],"answer":"Al-Biruni is a well-known scholar.","explanation":"Compound adjective before a noun → hyphen.","explanation_ar":"قبل الاسم ← شرطة."},{"q":"","options":["His books are-well known today.","His books are well-known-today.","His books are well known-today.","His books are well known today."],"answer":"His books are well known today.","explanation":"After be → usually no hyphen.","explanation_ar":"بعد be ← بلا شرطة."},{"q":"","options":["It's a highly efficient-engine.","It's a-highly efficient engine.","It's a highly efficient engine.","It's a highly-efficient engine."],"answer":"It's a highly efficient engine.","explanation":"-ly adverb + adjective → no hyphen.","explanation_ar":"بعد ly ← بلا شرطة."},{"q":"How do we write 47 in words?","options":["forty seven","four-ty seven","fortyseven","forty-seven"],"answer":"forty-seven","explanation":"Numbers 21–99 → hyphen.","explanation_ar":"الأعداد ← شرطة."},{"q":"","options":["Their daughter is six year-old.","Their daughter is six years old.","Their daughter is six-year-old.","Their daughter is six-years-old."],"answer":"Their daughter is six years old.","explanation":"a ten-year-old boy ↔ He is ten years old.","explanation_ar":"العمر."},{"q":"Which sentence is the least certain?","options":["Humans might live on Mars one day.","Humans will probably live on Mars one day.","Humans are going to live on Mars next week.","Humans will definitely live on Mars one day."],"answer":"Humans might live on Mars one day.","explanation":"Possible, not sure → may / might (not) + base verb.","explanation_ar":"الاحتمال ← may/might."},{"q":"Choose the best sentence for a text about the future.","options":["In 2040, people will probably be driving solar-powered cars that never need fuel.","In 2040, people will probably driving solar powered cars that never need fuel.","In 2040, people probably will to drive solar-powered cars that never need fuel.","In 2040, people will be probably drive solar-powered-cars that never need fuel."],"answer":"In 2040, people will probably be driving solar-powered cars that never need fuel.","explanation":"In progress at a future time → will be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل المستمر."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"this time tomorrow i will fly to a ten hour meeting in dubai.\"","options":["this time tomorrow, I'll be flying to a ten-hour meeting in dubai.","This time tomorrow, I'll be flying to a ten-hours meeting in Dubai.","This time tomorrow, I'll be flying to a ten-hour meeting in Dubai.","This time tomorrow, I will fly to a ten hour meeting in Dubai."],"answer":"This time tomorrow, I'll be flying to a ten-hour meeting in Dubai.","explanation":"In progress at a future time → will be + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل المستمر."},{"q":"What are you doing this weekend? – ___","options":["I going to visit my cousins in Abha.","I visit my cousins in Abha now.","I'll visiting my cousins in Abha.","I'm visiting my cousins in Abha."],"answer":"I'm visiting my cousins in Abha.","explanation":"Arrangement with time/people → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"الترتيب ← المضارع المستمر."}],"theme_ar":"عالم الغد","essential_question_ar":"كيف ستغيّر التكنولوجيا طريقة حياتنا؟","can_do":"I can make predictions with will, may and might, describe actions in progress in the future with the future continuous, choose the right future form, and use and punctuate compound adjectives.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أتنبأ بالمستقبل بـ will وmay وmight، وأصف أحداثًا مستمرة في المستقبل بالمستقبل المستمر، وأختار صيغة المستقبل المناسبة، وأستخدم الصفات المركبة وأضع لها الشرطة بشكل صحيح."});
